  'cape-town-level-1-water-restrictions-from-1-december-2026-11-16',
  'Cape Town brings in Level 1 water restrictions from 1 December',
  'Utilities', '2026-11-16', 'Cape Town ETC', 'https://www.capetownetc.com/news/level-one-water-restrictions/',
  'The City of Cape Town will apply Level 1 water restrictions from 1 December 2026 and wants everyone to use at least 10% less water over summer.',
  'The City of Cape Town has confirmed that Level 1 water restrictions start on 1 December 2026. The City ties the decision to the national water department''s yearly assessment of the Western Cape Water Supply System, which concluded that curbs are required.

Reports put storage across the dams at 70.4% as of 16 November, a gap of 13.4 percentage points compared with a year ago. Daily consumption reached 951 million litres, more than 91 million litres above the City''s target of 860 million litres. The City expects a longer, hotter and drier summer and asks residents, visitors and businesses to cut their water use by at least 10%.

Garden watering is limited to Tuesdays and Saturdays, for no more than an hour a day, and outside the hours from 09:00 to 18:00. That covers sprinklers, drip systems and trigger-nozzle hosepipes, and buckets and watering cans are bound by the same schedule. Sports fields and public parks may run sprinklers for one hour on Tuesdays and Fridays. Hosing down paved areas is not allowed, and the permanent Water By-law already keeps borehole and well-point users to the early-morning and evening windows.

Households are asked to aim for no more than 85 litres per person per day, covering hygiene, cooking, cleaning and laundry. Swimming pools may be filled and topped up but must be covered when not in use. Washing a car at home is still permitted with a bucket or low-volume pressure washer, and commercial car wash operators must reuse half or more of the water they use. The City says residents can apply for exemptions through its exemption process, and a full summary of the rules is on its water restrictions page.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.capetownetc.com/news/level-one-water-restrictions/", "https://smilefm.co.za/cape-town-confirms-level-1-water-restrictions-from-1-december/"]',
  'agent'
);
